BT /B 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 734 Tm (5. Slurm tools) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 713 Tm (a\) By default, a Slurm job on Euler begins execution in the directory from which sbatch was invoked,) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 698 Tm (unless another working directory is explicitly specified.) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 677 Tm (b\) SLURM_JOB_ID is an environment variable containing the unique job ID assigned by Slurm to the) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 662 Tm (running job.) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 641 Tm (c\) I can track my pending and running jobs using squeue -u "$USER".) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 620 Tm (d\) I can cancel a queued or running job using scancel JOB_ID.) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 599 Tm (e\) #SBATCH --gres=gpu:1 requests one GPU as a generic resource for each node allocated to the job.) Tj ET
BT /R 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 578 Tm (f\) #SBATCH --array=0-9 creates a job array with ten tasks indexed from 0 through 9.) Tj ET
